# Headers for what the asset server answers: the page, its script, its
# stylesheet and its fonts (#31). The build copies this file to the root
# of the assets, where wrangler reads it, under `wrangler dev` as in a
# deployment. The Worker's own answers, under /api/, are not assets and
# set their headers in code.
#
# Every source is this origin but one, and nothing inline or evaluated
# is allowed: the built page has neither, and a policy that allowed them
# would allow an injected script too.
#
# The one is Turnstile's (#32). A deployment that requires it has the
# page load Cloudflare's script from https://challenges.cloudflare.com,
# which draws its widget in a frame from there, so script-src and
# frame-src name that origin: the two directives Cloudflare documents
# the widget as needing, and no others. The token comes back to the
# page as a message from the frame, not a request of the page's, so
# connect-src stays this origin's alone. (The widget sends its own
# failure reports from the page to Cloudflare; those are refused, and
# the widget works without them.)
#
# Named whether a deployment turns Turnstile on or not. A policy that
# named it only when on would have to be written when the Worker
# starts: this file is served by the asset server, which never runs
# the Worker, and is built into the image before any setting is known.
# With Turnstile off the page never asks for the script, and what the
# allowance leaves open is one origin that serves Cloudflare's
# challenges and nothing else.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Named by their content, so a changed file is a new name and a cached
# one can be kept for good. Not set under /* as well: two rules naming
# one header are joined with a comma, and /assets/* matches both.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
